From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 19:14:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] vbscript: Take objects, Null and names as Windows does, and
 implement LoadPicture.

Measured on Windows 11 (build 29671):

- A built-in function given an object takes its default value, and
  getting that is the error: CStr, Len, Mid, CInt and the rest of a
  Dictionary answer 450, of a RegExp 438. IsObject, IsArray, IsDate,
  IsEmpty, IsNull, IsNumeric, TypeName, VarType and Array take the
  object itself; VarType answers the type of the default value where
  there is one.
- TypeName asks an object's IProvideClassInfo for its class first: a
  Scripting.Dictionary is "Dictionary", a Folder "Folder".
- Null is an invalid use of Null (94) to Chr, Sqr, String, StrReverse,
  Round and Rnd; Trim, LTrim and RTrim of Null are Null.
- Exp overflows with 6; CreateObject and GetObject of no name are an
  invalid procedure call (5); Split with a count of 0 splits into no
  substrings.
- Calling a name nothing declared, without Option Explicit, is a type
  mismatch (13), as in code run by Execute.
- LoadPicture loads a picture file into a Picture object; a missing
  file is error 432, a missing path or no name 76, and data that is no
  picture 481.
- The engine reports itself as VBScript 10.8.16384, and vbscript.dll's
  file version is 10.0.29671.1000.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 62b2634e2dcd614352592ec3be1ca068dd100651)

